<title>JAPAN: Asahi Bank battered by foreign investor selling.</title>
<headline>Asahi Bank battered by foreign investor selling.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-01-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Asahi Bank Ltd were sharply lower in Friday morning trade, battered by foreign investor selling, brokers said.</p>
<p>As of 0153 GMT, the shares were down 34 yen at 845 yen, the 13th largest percentage loser on the first section of the Tokyo bourse.  </p>
<p>&quot;The selling of Asahi Bank shares signifies that the recent flood of bank share sales by foreign investors is not over yet,&quot; said a deputy general manager at a second-tier brokerage.</p>
</text>
